# Canonical Turtle for the protocol-derived encoding of:
#   Qi‐Jun Hong et al. (2026). SLUSCHI-UP: A web infrastructure for SLUSCHI melting-temperature calculations using universal machine-learning interatomic potentials.
#   Computational Materials Science. doi:10.1016/j.commatsci.2026.115108  arXiv:2606.04973v1
#
# Version read: arxiv-preprint arXiv:2606.04973v1 (sha256 80d04250380a8dd0...);
#   the DOI above is cited, numbers are those of the version read.
# Corpus rank 175 (Application/model instance). Method identity follows
#   artifacts/kg/METHODS.md (registry: artifacts/kg/methods-registry.csv).
#
# Encoding scope: bibliographic facts only. SLUSCHI-UP is a web service
# that runs solid-liquid coexistence melting-temperature calculations
# with three deployed pretrained universal MLIPs (mace-mpa-0-medium,
# Allegro-OAM-L, DPA-3.2-5M-OMat24). The paper trains no model; its
# validation (MeltBench-10) is on melting temperatures. Read from the
# arXiv preprint (v1).

